<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fortress of Humaitá</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fortress of Humaitá was a Paraguayan fortification on a bend of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguay">Paraguay</a> River near its junction with the Paraná, guarding the river route to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asuncion">Asunción</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguayan-war">Paraguayan War</a> it held back the allied forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> for years, until Brazilian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ironclad">ironclads</a> forced their way past its batteries in February 1868. The garrison was cut off and the fortress fell in July 1868.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fortress-of-humaita.jpg" alt="Fortress of Humaitá" width="320" height="284" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: E.C. Jourdan (1838-1900) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Humaita_bend.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
